---
// BeyondTheBuild.astro — The Multidimensional Person Behind the Engineering
// Factual, sophisticated, restrained presentation of athletic, acoustic, creative, and exploratory background.
// Avoids childish emojis, maintains high-contrast engineering visual identity.
---

<section id="beyond" class="section beyond-section" aria-labelledby="beyondSectionHeading">
  <div class="container-wide">
    <!-- Section Header -->
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="header-kicker mono">[ 08 // BEYOND THE BUILD ]</div>
      <h2 id="beyondSectionHeading" class="section-title">
        The Person <span class="accent">Behind the Systems</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        "I like figuring out how things work — and then building them." Engineering is my primary professional identity, but physical endurance, acoustic rhythm, and visual storytelling directly shape how I lead, troubleshoot, and solve complex problems under pressure.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 4 Structured Dimension Pillars -->
    <div class="beyond-grid">
      
      <!-- PILLAR 1: MOVE (Athletics & Physical Training) -->
      <article class="beyond-card beyond-card-move">
        <div class="card-accent-strip"></div>
        <div class="card-head">
          <div class="card-meta mono">
            <span class="pillar-idx">01</span>
            <span class="pillar-category">PHYSICAL DISCIPLINE</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card-title">MOVE</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="spotlight-block">
          <span class="spotlight-badge mono">TRACK ATHLETICS</span>
          <p class="spotlight-text">
            <strong>"Before robotics, there was running."</strong> Competed in competitive sprint athletics during school years, progressing through district trials to represent at state-level running competitions.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="card-body">
          Regular strength training and competitive sports maintain the stamina and resilience required for 18-hour workshop fabrication marathons and rigorous track testing.
        </p>

        <div class="interests-cluster">
          <span class="cluster-label mono">ACTIVITIES &amp; DISCIPLINES</span>
          <div class="tag-cloud mono">
            <span class="tag-pill tag-priority">State-Level Track Athletics</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Strength Training &amp; Gym</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Football</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Cricket</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Badminton</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Basketball</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Volleyball</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Swimming</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Skateboarding</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Trekking &amp; Cycling</span>
            <span class="tag-pill tag-subtle">Jiu-Jitsu (Yellow Belt · School Years)</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- PILLAR 2: MUSIC (Choral Bass & Acoustic Expression) -->
      <article class="beyond-card beyond-card-music">
        <div class="card-accent-strip"></div>
        <div class="card-head">
          <div class="card-meta mono">
            <span class="pillar-idx">02</span>
            <span class="pillar-category">ACOUSTIC &amp; VOCAL</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card-title">MUSIC</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="spotlight-block">
          <span class="spotlight-badge mono">CHORAL BASS</span>
          <p class="spotlight-text">
            Active bass voice in a church choir for several years. Choral harmony instills precision listening, harmonic timing, and breath control that directly translates into vocal confidence during large-scale live anchoring and technical briefings.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="card-body">
          Music serves as an essential acoustic counterweight to hardware engineering. Primarily drawn to Western music (English) alongside expressive Malayalam and Hindi melodies.
        </p>

        <div class="interests-cluster">
          <span class="cluster-label mono">INSTRUMENTS &amp; REPERTOIRE</span>
          <div class="tag-cloud mono">
            <span class="tag-pill tag-priority">Church Choir (Bass Voice)</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Ukulele</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Drums</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Western Vocal</span>
            <span class="tag-pill tag-subtle">Aspiring: Electric Bass Guitar</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- PILLAR 3: CREATE (Digital Visuals & Hands-On Making) -->
      <article class="beyond-card beyond-card-create">
        <div class="card-accent-strip"></div>
        <div class="card-head">
          <div class="card-meta mono">
            <span class="pillar-idx">03</span>
            <span class="pillar-category">CREATIVE DIRECTION</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card-title">CREATE</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="spotlight-block">
          <span class="spotlight-badge mono">DIGITAL &amp; PHYSICAL CRAFT</span>
          <p class="spotlight-text">
            Extending engineering discipline into visual communication. Proficient in video assembly, technical slide architecture, visual graphics, and tactile physical DIY prototyping.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="card-body">
          Strong engineering requires clear translation. Creating intuitive technical presentations, documentation decks, and edited video demonstrations bridges complex robotic architectures with diverse stakeholders.
        </p>

        <div class="interests-cluster">
          <span class="cluster-label mono">SOFTWARE &amp; CREATIVE SKILLS</span>
          <div class="tag-cloud mono">
            <span class="tag-pill tag-priority">Video Editing (Filmora)</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Graphic Design (Photoshop &amp; Canva)</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">High-Impact Slide Decks (PowerPoint)</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Technical Photography</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Hands-on Wood &amp; Metal DIY</span>
            <span class="tag-pill tag-subtle">Culinary Craft</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- PILLAR 4: EXPLORE (Curiosity, Narratives & System Mastery) -->
      <article class="beyond-card beyond-card-explore">
        <div class="card-accent-strip"></div>
        <div class="card-head">
          <div class="card-meta mono">
            <span class="pillar-idx">04</span>
            <span class="pillar-category">INTELLECTUAL CURIOSITY</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card-title">EXPLORE</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="spotlight-block">
          <span class="spotlight-badge mono">SYSTEM INVESTIGATION</span>
          <p class="spotlight-text">
            An insatiable drive to dissect complex systems—whether mechanical teardowns on technical YouTube, expansive gaming systems like <em>Elden Ring</em> that demand patience and failure iteration, or off-grid mountain trekking.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="card-body">
          Long-term vision is grounded in pragmatic innovation: mastering deep robotics engineering today to eventually build products and venture initiatives that solve tangible, real-world societal problems.
        </p>

        <div class="interests-cluster">
          <span class="cluster-label mono">INTERESTS &amp; INSPIRATION</span>
          <div class="tag-cloud mono">
            <span class="tag-pill tag-priority">Technical YouTube &amp; Teardowns</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">High-Difficulty Gaming (Elden Ring)</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Travelling &amp; Mountain Trekking</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Anime &amp; Sci-Fi Cinema</span>
            <span class="tag-pill">Rock &amp; Alternative (Linkin Park)</span>
            <span class="tag-pill tag-subtle">Autonomous Hardware Ventures</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .beyond-section {
    background: transparent;
    padding-top: var(--section-pad);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-16);
    position: relative;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .beyond-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
  }

  .beyond-card {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--r-card);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-resting);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    transition: transform var(--dur-normal) var(--ease-out), box-shadow var(--dur-normal) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--dur-normal) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .beyond-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    box-shadow: 0 16px 36px -12px rgba(184, 146, 74, 0.18);
    border-color: var(--accent-primary, #B8924A);
  }

  .card-accent-strip {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 3px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent-primary, #B8924A), transparent);
    opacity: 0.65;
  }

  .card-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .card-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-2xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--accent-primary, #B8924A);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .pillar-idx {
    opacity: 0.65;
  }

  .card-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.5vw, 2.1rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--color-ink, #0E131F);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .spotlight-block {
    background: rgba(184, 146, 74, 0.06);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary, #B8924A);
    border-radius: 0 var(--r-sm) var(--r-sm) 0;
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .spotlight-badge {
    font-size: var(--text-3xs, 0.65rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--accent-primary, #B8924A);
  }

  .spotlight-text {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .card-body {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .interests-cluster {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .cluster-label {
    font-size: var(--text-3xs, 0.65rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .tag-cloud {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .tag-pill {
    font-size: var(--text-2xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: var(--r-full);
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .tag-priority {
    border-color: rgba(184, 146, 74, 0.45);
    background: rgba(184, 146, 74, 0.08);
    color: var(--accent-primary, #B8924A);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .tag-subtle {
    opacity: 0.75;
    font-size: 0.65rem;
  }

  .beyond-card:hover .tag-priority {
    background: rgba(184, 146, 74, 0.14);
    border-color: var(--accent-primary, #B8924A);
  }

  /* Responsive Layout */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .beyond-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }
    .beyond-card {
      padding: var(--space-6);
    }
  }
</style>
